### Must-fix, ranked

1. **P/PA native-20 versus exact endpoint contradiction:** calibration requires 20 native documents, but the exact 1,440-record domain permits only 15 per arm. Complete mixed-cohort coverage requires **1,680 records**, or an explicitly validated 1,440-record common view plus 240 native calibration records. Propagate coverage into timing and replay.
2. **Training versus evaluation crop:** v1.0 specifies donor-cropped training without a training-donor recipe; the existing training loop uses full real memory.
3. **Operational completeness:** bind model/tokenizer, initialization, donor, metric, path-validity, and artifact acceptance rules.
4. **Replay mechanics:** define diagnostic donor tensors and same-checkpoint reference-versus-reloaded comparisons—not just counts and hashes.
5. **Statistics and launch gates:** complete estimands, missing-data rules, fixture defaults, and D1/three-seed prerequisites.

Only the designated report was written. No training, evaluation, or tests were run. Golden hashes and preflight arithmetic were independently checked.

**No Phase 6, D0, D1, three-seed, B0-B/B1/B2/Stage C approval is granted. Test 163 remains sealed; P1 was unused; T5Gemma2 remains D-108 STOP.**
